#: {{syn|en|about|apropos|as for|Thesaurus:about}}
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Re A (conjoined twins)|'''Re''' A (conjoined twins)}} [2000] EWCA Civ 254}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=HarryBlank|work=w:SCP Foundation|title=SCP-5243|date=24 July 2020|url=https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5243|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240902172610/https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5243|archivedate=2 September 2024|accessdate=2 September 2024|text="I know it's been a long haul, but can we please not get complacent '''re:''' our annual magic gunk explosion? I can't believe I just typed those words."}}

=====Usage notes=====
This word, when used in this particular sense, is often rendered as ''Re:'' (with a colon and a capital R). Its capitalization in sentence-initial position (such as in subject lines) is often reanalyzed as being intrinsic, leading to intrasentence capitalization. Because email software introduces it to the subject line in email replies, it often conveys an added meaning of {{m|en|reply}} in the 21st century, in addition to the earlier aspect of {{m|en|regarding}}.

